{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cubiform-wooden-fruitbat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\nThe .bridge_state/projects.json write path VIOLATES the project invariant that every\ntickets-branch mutation must (1) run under the unified store write lock AND (2)\nauto-commit + auto-publish. projects_store.set_project/remove_project ->\nprojects_store._write_record is a bare tempfile+os.replace: no lock, no commit, no\npush. It also (a) hand-rolls atomic write instead of using the shared\nrebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write seam, and (b) accepts any project key with no\n_validate_project_key/existence guard. This is the mechanism that forced the ad-hoc\nhand-commits behind incident 05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27 (LEG/ONE/TWO/ZERO leak).\n\n## Existing seams we must use (do NOT reinvent)\n- rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write — the single crash-atomic write (umask/permissions/fsync).\n- The locked path-scoped commit+push composition, exemplified by\n  rebar._store.event_append.delete_events: _lock.write_lock(tracker, dual_window=True,\n  retries=_lock.write_path_retries()) -> _lock.check_no_rebase_in_progress(tracker)\n  (RebaseGuard) -> event_commit_git._git_commit_paths(tracker, msg, [relpath])\n  (path-scoped, never whole-index) -> push.push_tickets_branch(canonical). The\n  existing event writers (stage_and_commit/write_and_push) are event-dict-shaped and\n  do NOT fit a plain file, which is why a general facade is missing.\n\n## Approach\n1. Add ONE shared facade in rebar._store (e.g. event_append.write_and_push_paths(\n   tracker, relpaths, commit_msg) or a small new _store module) that, for arbitrary\n   already-written tickets-branch file paths, acquires write_lock + rebase guard,\n   _git_commit_paths the exact relpaths, restores-on-failure, and push_tickets_branch.\n   This is the missing choke point; model it on delete_events' locked body.\n2. Route projects_store writes: _write_record -> fsutil.atomic_write (verify byte-identical\n   output: json.dump(indent=2, sort_keys=True)+\"\\n\"), then set_project/remove_project\n   commit+push the projects.json relpath via the new facade so a mapping change is\n   durable + published without any hand-commit.\n3. Add write-time key validation: set_project calls fetcher._validate_project_key (or a\n   shared copy) and rejects syntactically-invalid keys with a clear non-zero error.\n4. Codify the two-part invariant in docs/concurrency.md (\"Mutating the tracker\" section):\n   EVERY tickets-branch mutation runs under write_lock AND auto-commits+publishes.\n\n## Constraints\n- BEHAVIOR-PRESERVING for the atomic-write swap: prove the on-disk bytes are identical\n  before/after (a RED test that pins the exact serialized bytes).\n- Preserve the ABSENT-record = legal-empty and MALFORMED = fail-closed semantics of\n  load_mapping unchanged.\n- Do NOT change resolve_project semantics here (legacy_default handling is ticket D).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. A projects.json mutation is committed to the tickets branch and pushed to sync.remote\n   under the unified write lock, with no ad-hoc git needed.\n2. projects_store uses fsutil.atomic_write; serialized bytes unchanged (pinned test).\n3. set_project rejects a syntactically-invalid key (e.g. \"le-g\", \"\", \"1x\") non-zero.\n4. docs/concurrency.md states the two-part invariant.\n5. Parity siblings (_commit_binding_store_snapshot, alert_store) are handled in ticket E\n   (this ticket provides the facade they will adopt).\n\n## Test plan\n- RED unit pinning projects.json serialized bytes across the atomic_write swap.\n- RED unit: set_project(\"le-g\", ...) raises/exits non-zero, no file written.\n- Unit asserting a mapping mutation acquires write_lock and calls _git_commit_paths +\n  push_tickets_branch (patch the seams; assert invoked) — the invariant regression.","id":"fea4-f98c-f1a2-4168","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Bridge-state writes: adopt shared locked commit+push + atomic_write seams; add projects.json key validation (tickets-branch invariant)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786807588199068001,"uuid":"65d86ae7-94c0-457a-a562-be8b09f4fa85"}